<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Buffels Q1 pre-capex net profit slides.</title>
<headline>Buffels Q1 pre-capex net profit slides.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Net profit before capital spending  11.85  vs  23.88</p>
<p>    Capital (recoupments)- net	    (2.38) vs  (6.00)</p>
<p>Gold output (kg)</p>
<p>    - underground			     1,586  vs  1,491</p>
<p>    - surface				     376  vs  441</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    - underground			    233,000 vs 219,000</p>
<p>    - surface				  451,000 vs 469,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    - underground				6.81  vs 6.81</p>
<p>    - surface				    0.83  vs 0.94</p>
<p>Cost (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    - underground			     44,898 vs 47,871</p>
<p>    - surface				   27,274 vs 23,635</p>
<p>Full name: Buffelsfontein Gold Mining Co Ltd, managed by Randgold and Exploration Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Capital expenditure planned for the June quarter amounts to 10.0 million rand for the installation of the new Mill and C.I.P. plant.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
